questions.q:
The mean deviation of the following data about its mean is
\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|l|l|}
\hlinex_i & 5 & 15 & 25 & 35 & 45 \\
\hlinef_i & 8 & 48 & 56 & 32 & 16 \\
\hline
\end{array}

questions.solution:
Given, scores 505, 510, 515, 520, ... 595 the mean of these 19 scores $=550=\bar{X}$
So,

\begin{aligned}
\sum_{i=1}^{19}\left(x_i-\bar{x}\right)^2 & =2\left(45^2+40^2+35^2+\ldots+5^2\right) \\
& =2 \times 5^2 \times\left[1^2+2^2+3^2+\ldots+9^2\right]
\end{aligned}

So, standard derivation

=\sqrt{\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{19}\left(x_i-\bar{x}\right)^2}{n}}=\sqrt{\frac{2 \times 5^2 \times \frac{9 \times 10 \times 19}{6}}{19}}=5 \sqrt{30}

